:: Keyboard Shortcuts
Keyboard shortcuts for [[SugarCube 2|https://www.motoslave.net/sugarcube/2/]] stories which players can rebind in a settings dialog. Requires SugarCube v2.37.0 or later. It's embedded here, so feel free to try it out.

OOB features:
* <kbd>←</kbd> / <kbd>→</kbd> for history navigation
* <kbd>Space</kbd> for passages with a single link (after scrolling to the bottom)
* <kbd>1</kbd>–<kbd>5</kbd> and <kbd>Q</kbd>–<kbd>T</kbd> for the first ten links of a passage. Each one is annotated with a small hint like {{{[1]}}}. The <kbd>6</kbd>–<kbd>0</kbd> keys can be used instead of <kbd>Q</kbd>–<kbd>T</kbd> as well as the numpad numbers.

!!!Installation
The package ships three files in {{{dist/}}}:
* {{{hotkey.js}}} has to go into the Story JavaScript //before// any code using the {{{Hotkey}}} global
* {{{hotkey.css}}} goes into the Story Stylesheet
* {{{hotkey.d.ts}}} declares the {{{Hotkey}}} global for your editor, e.g. via {{{/// <reference types="@spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey" />}}}

!!!!Tweego
Add the package via your favourite package manager:
{{{
yarn add --dev @spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey
# or
npm install -S -D @spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey
}}}
Include the plugin sources in your tweego invocation before your own:
{{{
tweego -o index.html node_modules/@spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey/dist src
}}}

!!!!Twine
Copy the contents of [[hotkey.js|https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey/dist/hotkey.js]] to the top of your Story JavaScript and [[hotkey.css|https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@spectreforge/sugarcube-hotkey/dist/hotkey.css]] into your Story Stylesheet.

!!!Usage
{{{
Hotkey.initialize();
}}}
That's it. A "Keyboard Settings" item will be added to the UI bar and the players' changed bindings will be persisted with SugarCube's settings.

!!!!Custom actions
{{{
Hotkey.initialize({
	actions: {
		inventory: { type: "link-click", name: "Open Inventory" },
		journal: {
			type: "invoke",
			name: "Open Journal",
			handle: () => Engine.play("Journal"),
		},
	},
	keymap: { KeyI: "inventory", KeyJ: "journal" },
	hints: { inventory: Hotkey.AUTO_HINT },
});
}}}
Shortcuts are physical keys ({{{KeyboardEvent.code}}}) with optional modifiers in the order {{{Meta+Ctrl+Alt+Shift}}}, e.g. {{{Ctrl+Shift+KeyS}}}. Browser and assistive technology shortcuts like <kbd>Tab</kbd> or <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>R</kbd> can't be bound.

A {{{link-click}}} action clicks the first visible and enabled link marked with it:
{{{
<<hotlink-to "inventory" "Inventory">>
<<hotlink-to "inventory" [[Inventory][$from = passage()]]>>
<<hotlink "inventory">><<link "Inventory">>...<</link>><</hotlink>>
}}}
All options are documented in {{{hotkey.d.ts}}}.

!!!!Opting out
* {{{nohotkey}}} passage tag: no shortcuts and no hints on this passage
* {{{nohotkey-implicit}}} passage tag: no numbered links on this passage
* {{{data-hotkey-noimplicit}}} attribute: excludes a link (or all links within the element) from numbering
* {{{implicitActions: false}}} option: no numbered links at all

!!!Localization
All UI strings are {{{l10nStrings}}} entries prefixed with {{{hotkey}}}, see {{{DEFAULT_STRINGS}}} in [[hotkey-l10n.ts|https://github.com/spectreforge/sugarshock/blob/main/packages/hotkey/src/hotkey-l10n.ts]]. Assign your translations before calling {{{Hotkey.initialize()}}}, or call it again afterwards.

!!!Theming
The settings dialog derives its colours from the surrounding text colour and can be adjusted via a few CSS custom properties which are documented at the top of {{{hotkey.css}}}.
